cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use, cite or build on this work, please cite it as below."
type: report
title: "A5K — An Amiga-Inspired Deterministic Display and Audio Card"
version: "Rev. AW"
date-released: "2026-11-04"
license: CC-BY-4.0
authors:
  - name: 'Ryan David Hall (AKA "ProphetPX")'
abstract: >-
  A design study for a deterministic PCIe display and audio engine inspired by
  the Amiga custom chipset: an Agnus-class slot scheduler, a planar
  Denise-class scanout, a minterm blitter and an MC-1 Copper, with a published
  slot-exact timing contract. It is not an Amiga clone and claims no binary
  compatibility. Includes a Copper instruction set, a simulator specification,
  a bill of materials and a comparative analysis against AAA, Hombre and a
  2026 scientific workstation.
keywords:
  - Amiga
  - open hardware
  - FPGA
  - RISC-V
  - Copper
  - display architecture
